{"parentUuid":"f15c8481-1c10-4615-b2f5-2252ab366154","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FyjiiPd2j7qXNTiumSzs7K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H82CdoEKMaXVeAfUDnT1xK","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CAMBranch imitation learning branch and bound MILP 2024"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7213,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":152,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7213},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7213,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyTfSyxjaQt6NDrA3Xf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0a9fe9b3-495f-43de-8617-443f0128bb9d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:51.319Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0a9fe9b3-495f-43de-8617-443f0128bb9d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H82CdoEKMaXVeAfUDnT1xK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CAMBranch imitation learning branch and bound MILP 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=K6kt50zAiG&noteId=eAKTDVd6fy\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.03647] CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.03647v1] CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647v1\"},{\"title\":\"CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.03647\"},{\"title\":\"Machine learning augmented branch and bound for mixed integer linear programming | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02130-y\"},{\"title\":\"Paper page - CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2402.03647\"},{\"title\":\"Learning efficient branch-and-bound for solving Mixed Integer Linear Programs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625001747\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Imitation Learning to Branch for MIP: A Hybrid Reinforcement Learning based Sample Augmentation Approach | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=NdcQQ82mfy\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.05501] Machine Learning Augmented Branch and Bound for Mixed Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.05501\"},{\"title\":\"A Markov Decision Process for Variable Selection in Branch & Bound\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.19348\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CAMBranch:\n\n## CAMBranch Overview\n\nCAMBranch is a framework that generates Augmented MILPs (AMILPs) by applying variable shifting to limited expert data from their original MILPs. The paper was submitted on February 6, 2024, and appears in multiple academic sources including arXiv and OpenReview.\n\n## Core Problem and Solution\n\nMachine learning frameworks have been introduced to enhance Branch and Bound (B&B) branching policies for solving Mixed Integer Linear Programming (MILP), primarily relying on imitation learning of Strong Branching. However, collecting expert samples for imitation learning, particularly for Strong Branching, is a time-consuming endeavor.\n\n## How CAMBranch Works\n\nCAMBranch leverages both MILPs and AMILPs for imitation learning and employs contrastive learning to enhance the model's ability to capture MILP features, thereby improving the quality of branching decisions.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nExperimental results demonstrate that CAMBranch, trained with only 10% of the complete dataset, exhibits superior performance. The research addresses a practical challenge in applying machine learning to MILP solving by significantly reducing the data requirements needed for effective imitation learning while maintaining competitive performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f9aad8ef-5567-4e2d-8e8d-b6b0295a427a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:57.448Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0a9fe9b3-495f-43de-8617-443f0128bb9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f15c8481-1c10-4615-b2f5-2252ab366154","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnAhTjGGdj9kh9JA1o1BGV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"imitation learning behavior cloning SAT solver branching 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25411\"},{\"title\":\"[2509.25411] Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25411\"},{\"title\":\"[Quick Review] Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://liner.com/review/boolean-satisfiability-via-imitation-learning\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/396048817_Boolean_Satisfiability_via_Imitation_Learning\"},{\"title\":\"Behavioral Cloning (BC) - imitation\",\"url\":\"https://imitation.readthedocs.io/en/latest/algorithms/bc.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2407.15007] Is Behavior Cloning All You Need? Understanding Horizon in Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.15007\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Behavior Cloning with Action Quantization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.20538\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=LNqWbY5iIf\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Imitation Learning & the Behavior Cloning Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://wensun.github.io/CS4789_data/Imitation_Learning_April_8_annotated.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found highly relevant research on this topic:\n\n## ImitSAT: Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\n\nImitSAT is the first branching policy for CDCL solvers based on imitation learning. This is a recent development in applying machine learning to SAT solving.\n\n**Key Innovation:**\n\nImitSAT is a branching policy for conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL) solvers based on imitation learning for the Boolean satisfiability problem (SAT). Unlike previous methods that predict instance-level signals to improve CDCL branching indirectly, or rely on reinforcement learning and insufficient CDCL information to enhance branching, ImitSAT learns from expert KeyTrace that collapses a full run into the sequence of surviving decisions.\n\n**Supervision Mechanism:**\n\nReplaying a KeyTrace on the same instance is nearly conflict-free, providing dense decision-level supervision and directly reducing propagations—the dominant contributor to wall-clock time. This prefix-conditioned supervision enables ImitSAT to reproduce high-quality branches without exploration, yielding faster convergence, stable training, and seamless integration into CDCL.\n\n**Performance Results:**\n\nExtensive experiments demonstrate that ImitSAT reduces propagation counts and runtime, outperforming state-of-the-art learned approaches. More specifically, ImitSAT consistently outperforms Graph-Q-SAT and SATformer in reducing propagation counts on held-out random 3-SAT test sets across most variable ranges, achieving the lowest Median Relative Propagation Percentage (MRPP). For instance, with 5 calls, ImitSAT achieves an MRPP of 0.66 on 50 variables, significantly lower than SATformer's 0.88 and Graph-Q-SAT's 0.70.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a1e51c89-b2a7-45f1-82a8-48d63b8d7c33","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:01.571Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f15c8481-1c10-4615-b2f5-2252ab366154","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
