{"parentUuid":"2727d845-fc8e-470f-8d73-4a38cd8bd3be","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ss2MVCLodh8jMangVRdqfk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lifzt3wsNCVrG6UZSDh39B","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"DAgger vs behavior cloning combinatorial optimization branching 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1505,"cache_read_input_tokens":20334,"output_tokens":158,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1505},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1224,"output_tokens":158,"cache_read_input_tokens":20334,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1505,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyUiCwtBKja56CZPBcz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b183d197-cdac-4f29-8ddb-80e96de942a5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:04.412Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2727d845-fc8e-470f-8d73-4a38cd8bd3be","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHJ5DaZ4CVLURUrAXSgwow","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Khalil strong branching imitation learning 2024 2025 follow-up\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learning in Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.03626v1\"},{\"title\":\"Learning in Reformulation-Linearization Technique-Based Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2024.0775\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - INFORMSJoC/2024.0775\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/INFORMSJoC/2024.0775\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Learning in Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381227571_Learning_in_Spatial_Branching_Limitations_of_Strong_Branching_Imitation\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25411\"},{\"title\":\"arXiv:2408.14774v4 [cs.LG] 28 May 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.14774\"},{\"title\":\"Empowering branch-and-bound algorithms via reinforcement and imitation learning for enhanced search - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625000018\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Interactive imitation learning for dexterous robotic manipulation: challenges and perspectives—a survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/robotics-and-ai/articles/10.3389/frobt.2025.1682437/full\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025 INSTRUCT-SKILLMIX:\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/file/473a9a75edc46eff5ff224d53d5f7294-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Model Predictive Adversarial Imitation Learning for Planning from Observation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.21533v1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant research on strong branching imitation learning. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Main Research Finding\n\nA 2025 paper by González-Rodríguez, Gómez-Casares, Ghaddar, González-Díaz, and Pateiro-López titled \"Learning in Reformulation-Linearization Technique-Based Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\" was published in the INFORMS Journal on Computing.\n\n## Background on Strong Branching Imitation\n\nKhalil et al. (2016) explored an online framework that ranks variables to replicate strong branching, while Gasse et al. (2019) used offline learning to encode branching policies into a graph convolutional neural network for fast approximations of strong branching.\n\n## Key Challenges Identified\n\nThe recent work addresses important limitations in the field. The claim that strong branching is a desirable strategy to follow has recently been challenged, with some instances where strong branching scores provide no useful information. Standard implementations of strong branching can identify infeasibilities and provide faster dual-bound improvements in ways that no rule aimed at imitating strong branching can achieve.\n\nAdditionally, strong branching relies on the LP relaxation for scoring variables, which can provide little information in cases when the optimal LP objective value does not change with branching.\n\nThe software supporting the 2025 study is available in the paper and its supplemental information as well as from the IJOC GitHub software repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"614f5d24-7302-44ad-9510-e65b72115c79","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:11.257Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2727d845-fc8e-470f-8d73-4a38cd8bd3be","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b183d197-cdac-4f29-8ddb-80e96de942a5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lifzt3wsNCVrG6UZSDh39B","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DAgger vs behavior cloning combinatorial optimization branching 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Behavioral Cloning (BC) - imitation\",\"url\":\"https://imitation.readthedocs.io/en/latest/algorithms/bc.html\"},{\"title\":\"DAgger - imitation\",\"url\":\"https://imitation.readthedocs.io/en/latest/algorithms/dagger.html\"},{\"title\":\"imitation-learning-tutorials/02_dagger.ipynb at master · tsmatz/imitation-learning-tutorials\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tsmatz/imitation-learning-tutorials/blob/master/02_dagger.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"Dataset Aggregation (DAgger) in Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/dataset-aggregation-dagger\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - rudolfsteiner/DAgger: Reinforcement Learning -- Imitation Learning, Behavior Cloning, DAgger (Data Aggregation) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rudolfsteiner/DAgger\"},{\"title\":\"Imitation Learning using Reward-Guided DAgger\",\"url\":\"https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1508210/FULLTEXT01.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Behavioral Cloning and Imitation Learning for Autonomous Driving | by Paichun Jim Lin | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@paichul/building-driving-assist-system-part-1-f7fb9278670c\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Inverse RL: BC and DAgger. | Hill Climbing\",\"url\":\"https://blog.wz-ml.com/Behavioral-Cloning-and-Dagger/\"},{\"title\":\"[1810.02890] HG-DAgger: Interactive Imitation Learning with Human Experts\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.02890\"},{\"title\":\"Berkeley CS 285 Deep Reinforcement Learning, Decision Making, and Control\",\"url\":\"https://rail.eecs.berkeley.edu/deeprlcourse/static/homeworks/hw1.pdf\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Summary of Search Results\n\nThe search returned information about DAgger (Dataset Aggregation) and behavioral cloning in imitation learning, with some 2025 research developments:\n\n**Key Differences:**\n- DAgger iteratively trains a policy using supervised learning on expert demonstrations, runs the policy to gather observations, queries the expert for actions on those observations, and adds newly labeled observations to the dataset—improving on behavioral cloning by training on a dataset that better resembles the observations the trained policy is likely to encounter, but it requires querying the expert online.\n\n- Behavioral cloning is a simple approach to learning a policy, but the policy often generalizes poorly and does not recover well from errors.\n\n**2025 Research:**\nRecent advances include Compliant Residual DAgger which yielded absolute success gains of 50–60 percentage points in book-flipping and belt assembly tasks (2025). Additionally, ASkDAgger incorporates active skill-level gating to modulate query frequencies, cutting annotation effort by 30–50% (2025).\n\n**Current Status:**\nDAgger remains consistently dominant over classical behavioral cloning, with further gains in sample efficiency, safety, and robustness arising from recent algorithmic innovations.\n\nHowever, the search results did not contain specific information about DAgger vs. behavior cloning in the context of combinatorial optimization or branching problems specifically. You may need additional searches for those particular application areas.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"93d84179-57c7-4b89-a697-d9afa506d717","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:12.118Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b183d197-cdac-4f29-8ddb-80e96de942a5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
