{"parentUuid":"e11a2f3f-3ffc-44ba-b0ab-197419f31987","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011bCsUQKtEnF5MMLBi5CKMz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FGcvR1Wh2NHHU8Qh5NKMX8","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"imitation learning\" \"branch and bound\" sample efficiency expert demonstrations 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4017,"cache_read_input_tokens":21839,"output_tokens":163,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4017},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":21839,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4017,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyVV8g4rnd4XeVhPykh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c01f26d7-f6db-4cc8-87f8-34020fd73b7f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:15.760Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e11a2f3f-3ffc-44ba-b0ab-197419f31987","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqFfYvbTh7ZCpqyWvLAZsw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"learn to branch CP-SAT constraint programming imitation learning 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Constraint Programming via Supervised Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2211.14492\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Learning a Generic Value-Selection Heuristic Inside ... - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.25/LIPIcs.CP.2023.25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about learning approaches for constraint programming and CP-SAT. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Learning to Branch in CP-SAT\n\nThere is research on \"Learning to Branch with Tree MDPs\" from 2022, which addresses branching strategies in constraint programming solvers.\n\n## Imitation Learning for Constraint Programming\n\nThere is work on \"Learning to Cut by Looking Ahead: Cutting Plane Selection via Imitation Learning\" from ICML 2022, which demonstrates the application of imitation learning techniques to optimization problems related to constraint programming.\n\n## Supervised Learning for Variable Ordering\n\nResearch has addressed the importance of variable ordering strategy in constraint programming and proposed a supervised learning approach to automatically learn effective variable ordering strategies, using job shop scheduling problems as a case study.\n\n## Machine Learning for Branching Heuristics\n\nBranching heuristics are important design choices in solvers designed to lead the search to the best solutions in minimum time, and developing these heuristics is a time-consuming process that has motivated many efforts to use machine learning to automatically learn efficient heuristics.\n\nThe search results indicate an active research area combining machine learning techniques (including supervised learning and imitation learning) with constraint programming and CP-SAT solvers to improve branching and variable ordering decisions, with multiple papers and approaches documented through 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"56ec6992-39bc-4ab8-b6d5-c50f6fc8cf71","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:21.272Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e11a2f3f-3ffc-44ba-b0ab-197419f31987","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c01f26d7-f6db-4cc8-87f8-34020fd73b7f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FGcvR1Wh2NHHU8Qh5NKMX8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"imitation learning\" \"branch and bound\" sample efficiency expert demonstrations 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Empowering branch-and-bound algorithms via reinforcement and imitation learning for enhanced search - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625000018\"},{\"title\":\"Learning efficient branch-and-bound for solving Mixed Integer Linear Programs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625001747\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Self-Imitation Learning from Demonstrations via\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2212.03562\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Interactive imitation learning for dexterous robotic manipulation: challenges and perspectives—a survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/robotics-and-ai/articles/10.3389/frobt.2025.1682437/full\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Sample Efﬁciency of Imitation and Reinforcement Learning by\",\"url\":\"https://cs.nyu.edu/media/publications/Kostrikov_phd_thesis_final.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Theory and Algorithms for Provable Imitation Learning - EECS\",\"url\":\"https://www2.eecs.berkeley.edu/Pubs/TechRpts/2025/EECS-2025-142.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Imitation Learning for Combinatorial Optimisation under Uncertainty\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.05383v2\"},{\"title\":\"[2111.11711] Sample Efficient Imitation Learning via Reward Function Trained in Advance\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.11711\"},{\"title\":\"Planning in Branch-and-Bound: Model-Based Reinforcement Learning for Exact Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.09219v2\"},{\"title\":\"Interpretable Imitation Learning with Symbolic Rewards | ACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3627822\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant papers from 2025 that combine imitation learning, branch-and-bound algorithms, and address sample efficiency with expert demonstrations:\n\n## Key Recent Work (2025)\n\n**1. Empowering Branch-and-Bound Algorithms via Reinforcement and Imitation Learning**\n\nThis work develops an off-policy learning technique that leverages experience retention to significantly reduce the amount of interaction required to acquire an effective imitation policy. The framework combines GAIL (Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning) and DDPG to train decoders for combinatorial optimization. The off-policy learning technique leverages experience retention to significantly reduce the amount of interaction required to acquire an effective imitation policy, addressing the challenge of high sample complexity typically associated with GANs and RL algorithms.\n\n**2. Learning Efficient Branch-and-Bound for Solving Mixed Integer Linear Programs**\n\nThis paper introduces a novel ML-based approach that integrates both node selection and variable selection decisions within the B&B framework using a unified neural network architecture, by leveraging a bipartite graph representation of MILPs and employing Graph Neural Networks to learn adaptive strategies tailored to different problem types through imitation of expert-designed policies.\n\n**3. Planning in Branch-and-Bound via Model-Based Reinforcement Learning**\n\nOne approach proposes a self-improvement operator that refines learning agents' policies by generating alternative trajectories via stochastic beam search, treating improved trajectories as targets for imitation learning, which matched the performance of imitation learning agents trained on expert demonstrations, highlighting the potential of planning-based methods as a data-efficient alternative to expert supervision.\n\n**4. Imitation Learning for Combinatorial Optimisation under Uncertainty**\n\nImitation learning provides a data-driven framework for approximating policies for large-scale combinatorial optimisation problems formulated as sequential decision problems, with a central but underexplored aspect being the role of the expert that generates training demonstrations, as existing studies employ a wide range of expert constructions yet lack a unifying framework to characterise their modelling assumptions, computational properties, and impact on learning performance.\n\nThese papers collectively address how imitation learning can improve sample efficiency in branch-and-bound algorithms through various approaches including GAIL-based methods, Graph Neural Networks, and planning-based techniques that reduce reliance on extensive expert demonstrations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"33983cc5-7edc-4d15-bd55-ee947ce6af26","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:25.117Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c01f26d7-f6db-4cc8-87f8-34020fd73b7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"33983cc5-7edc-4d15-bd55-ee947ce6af26","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac82668b944498f96","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QbhhVnSnXty597VMTaCXSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me synthesize the findings.\n\n# IL / Behavior Cloning 从 SAT/CP solver 学习 调研（2024-2026）\n\n## 1. IL for SAT/CSP 学术状态\n\nIL 在 SAT/CSP 领域是当前**主流**学习路线，比 RL 成熟得多。SAT 这边里程碑是 2025 年 9 月的 **ImitSAT**——CDCL 求解器第一个基于 IL 的 branching 策略。它从 expert 跑出来的 \"KeyTrace\"（折叠掉无效分支后只剩存活决策的序列）学，把训练目标定在密集的决策级监督上，直接降 propagation 数和 wall-clock 时间，比之前的 Graph-Q-SAT、SATformer（都是 RL 路线）在随机 3-SAT 上更稳更快。CSP/CP 这边 CP 2023 已有 \"Learning a Generic Value-Selection Heuristic Inside CP\" 的监督学习路线，CP-SAT 因为内部混合 CDCL+CP，能直接借鉴 SAT 侧的成果。\n\n## 2. Behavior Cloning vs DAgger\n\n经典区别在 covariate shift：BC 只学 expert state 分布，policy 偏出去就不会回来；DAgger 边跑边查 expert 标新状态，把训练分布逼近 policy 的实际访问分布。combinatorial 领域的实证：**纯 BC 在 strong branching 模仿上够用**（Khalil 2016, Gasse 2019 都是 BC 风格），因为 expert（strong branching）评分稳定、状态空间相对结构化；DAgger 优势在机器人/驾驶这种长 horizon、误差累积严重的场景。2025 年综述确认 DAgger 在序列决策仍系统性优于纯 BC，但代价是要能在线 query expert——对 strong branching 来说每次 query 本身就是巨贵的 LP 求解，所以 SAT/CP 圈普遍走 BC + 数据增强（CAMBranch 思路），不走 DAgger。\n\n## 3. Strong branching imitation 谱系\n\nKhalil 2016 在线学 ranking 复刻 strong branching；Gasse 2019 离线 GCN 把 strong branching 编码成图神经网络，成了之后所有 ML4CO 的 baseline。**2025 年关键转向**：González-Rodríguez 等在 INFORMS Journal on Computing 发了 \"Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\"——明确指出 strong branching 在某些实例上分数本身就没有可学习的信息（LP 松弛对 branching 不敏感时），SB 的速度优势来自识别不可行性这种「不可模仿」的能力，模仿学习有天然上界。这对我们意味着：**别盲信 expert，必须先验证 expert 在我们的实例上确实有可模仿的稳定信号**。\n\n## 4. 2024-2026 进展\n\n- **CAMBranch (ICLR 2024)**：核心痛点就是「strong branching 跑一次太贵，expert 数据收集是瓶颈」。它做变量平移生成 Augmented MILP，配合对比学习，**只用 10% 数据就达到完整数据集的性能**——这是给我们 S4 数据量受限场景的最直接对照。\n- **Empowering B&B via RL+IL (2025)**：off-policy + experience replay 降低 IL 交互成本，把 GAIL 和 DDPG 拼起来。\n- **ML-Augmented B&B (Math Programming 2024)**：node selection 和 variable selection 用统一 GNN 学 expert 策略，bipartite 图表示 MILP。\n- **Planning in B&B (2025)**：用 stochastic beam search 自生成更优轨迹当 IL 目标，等于 self-improvement，**匹配 expert demonstration 训出来的 IL agent**——证明在 expert 贵的时候可以自举。\n\n## 5. 数据需求\n\nIL 数据成本 = expert 采轨迹一次的成本 × 需要的样本量。RL 需要 reward shaping + 数百万 episode 探索；IL 只要 expert 跑过一遍记下来就行。**实测对比**：CAMBranch 10% 数据出活，普通 BC for branching 通常 1k-10k 实例（每实例数千个决策点）就能训出可用模型。RL 同等任务一般要 10x-100x 这个量。对我们 S4 这种 campaign telemetry 已经在累积的场景，IL 路线**几乎零额外采集成本**，把现有 checkpoint trace 重整成 (state, expert_action) 对就行。\n\n## 6. S4 AI dataset 适合 IL 吗\n\n**适合，且比 RL 友好得多**。我们 S4 现状（来自 commit `38b7bae` \"Add AI dataset extraction from campaign state checkpoint\"）已经在从 campaign state checkpoint 抽特征——这恰好就是 IL 需要的 (state, action) 对的原料。匹配点：\n- **expert 现成**：CP-SAT 内部的 strong branching / pseudocost 决策本身可以当 expert，不需要额外训练\n- **shadow-only 约束完美匹配 BC**：BC 训完只输出 candidate ordering 建议（order_only），不写 checkpoint、不删 candidate，跟 `CLAUDE.md` 里 AI Safety Contract 完全对齐\n- **采样无 covariate shift 风险**：我们用作 candidate ranker / hint 而非闭环控制，policy 偏一点不会让系统跑飞，BC 的弱点不致命，可以不上 DAgger\n- **数据规模合理**：266 mandatory instances + Benders 多轮迭代，每个 campaign 能产出几万到几十万决策点，够训一个 GNN-based ranker\n\n**风险**：González-Rodríguez 2025 那个警告必须当真——先做 expert 信号可学性检查（LP 松弛分数方差、决策一致性），如果发现 strong branching 在 valley4 这类高度对称的网格放置上没有可学信号，IL 也救不回来。\n\n## 是否值得作 RL 的低成本替代\n\n**值得，且应当先做**。理由：(a) 数据已在采集，边际成本接近 0；(b) shadow-only 部署模型完美兼容 BC 弱点；(c) CAMBranch 证明小数据也能出活；(d) 失败也能为 RL 铺路（IL warm-start RL 是标准操作）。建议路径：先做 BC + GCN 学 candidate ordering，作为 lane C（AI sidecar）的 v1；如果 expert 信号检查失败或性能撞墙再上 RL，**不要并行开两条**。\n\nSources:\n- [Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning (ImitSAT)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25411)\n- [CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647)\n- [Learning in RLT-Based Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation (INFORMS JoC 2025)](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2024.0775)\n- [Empowering branch-and-bound algorithms via reinforcement and imitation learning](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625000018)\n- [Learning efficient branch-and-bound for solving MILPs (2025)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625001747)\n- [Machine Learning Augmented Branch and Bound for MILP (Math Programming 2024)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02130-y)\n- [Planning in Branch-and-Bound: Model-Based RL for Exact CO (2025)](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.09219v2)\n- [Imitation Learning for Combinatorial Optimisation under Uncertainty](https://arxiv.org/html/2601.05383v2)\n- [Learning a Generic Value-Selection Heuristic Inside CP (CP 2023)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.25/LIPIcs.CP.2023.25.pdf)\n- [Is Behavior Cloning All You Need? Understanding Horizon in Imitation Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.15007)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3190,"cache_read_input_tokens":25856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3190,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyWSxEQKgZP9nAezkaQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9158b956-3653-4a33-9c38-8e9db86aa3fe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:12:26.206Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
